## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | lib/src/cli/provider_models.dart | 🚨 blocking modelinputmodalities survives provider switches — stale cross provider modality verdicts are applied at model switches the new cache is only overwritten when the new endpoint reports modalities — if modalities isnotempty modelinputmodalities modalities here and in fetchcopilotmodels provider models dart 951 — so an endpoint that answers without modality metadata plain openai compatible codemie copilot — the copilot dialect always returns an empty modality map leaves the previous provider s map in place and no provider session switch clears it five reset sites clear the sibling caches with the comment the cached model list belongs to the previous provider endpoint and modelinputmodalities is missing from all of them lib src cli provider models dart 1379 1381 lib src cli provider commands dart 2066 2067 and 2126 2127 lib src cli codemie provider commands dart 381 382 lib src cli provider codemie sso dart 224 225 lib src cli session commands dart 1992 1993 switchinputmodalities provider models dart 1047 then consults the stale map first repro connect ain models reports claude → text image → switch to an endpoint without modality fields whose list shares any id with the ain answer gateways commonly proxy the same upstream ids → model id saves the model with the ain verdict s input modalities wrong input on the active model is exactly the defect class gh 2466 fixes — reintroduced via provider switching fix clear modelinputmodalities const at the five reset points mirroring modelcontextwindows modelmaxtokens and or drop the isnotempty guard in fetchopenaicompatiblemodels so a fresh answer always replaces the map that path already assigns windows caps unconditionally |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/lib/services/aiin_connect_flow.dart | ⚠️ important the ain app connect flow never passes supportsimages — the added parameter is inert the onboarding config still derives vision from the name heuristic registeraiinprovider gained bool supportsimages and forwards it into the reconnect config but its only call site finishaiinconnect aiin connect flow dart 736 745 does not pass it and pickaiinmodel returns only the chosen id — the v1 models payload with its input modalities is discarded at aiin connect flow dart 829 1 so a user onboarding through the ain connect flow who picks a heuristic invisible multimodal id mistralai mistral large 4 0 meta muse still gets supportsimages null → modelidsuggestsvision heuristic → the image attachment lock gh 2466 2 targets stays locked on this surface the pr description lists agentconfig supportsimages in the ain app flow among the wired surfaces — as shipped only the settings form s custom provider flow settings flows dart 386 covered by flutter app test endpoint modalities vision test dart and the pickers derive vision from endpoint modalities fix return the fetched info from the model pick or re look the id up in fetchmodelsforendpoint aiindefaultchatbaseurl 4 and pass modalities modelid contains image into registeraiinprovider add the connect flow case to flutter app test endpoint modalities vision test dart |
| F3 | open | IMPORTANT | packages/fa_ui/lib/src/providers/unified_model_picker.dart | ⚠️ important the supportsimages doc comment states the opposite of the implemented precedence the doc says a false never overrides a heuristic true — an endpoint that answers modalities at all is more specific than a name matcher but the implementation below does exactly the override it forbids dart bool get visioncapable supportsimages modelidsuggestsvision modelid with supportsimages false endpoint reported text returns false — overriding a heuristic true e g gpt 4o shaped ids every other surface in this pr implements endpoint wins including false settings dart onmodelidchanged a reported text only list unchecks it the cli s switchinputmodalities and the pr description itself prefer endpoint modalities with the heuristic as fallback so the code is right and the comment is wrong — and this precedence is the crux rule of gh 2466 so the next reader may fix the code to match the comment and invert it fix reword the doc to a reported verdict wins true or false only null falls back to the id heuristic |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

